      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>In Scotland the Care Inspectorate regulates care services. CQC applies in England only; Care Inspectorate Wales and RQIA in Northern Ireland run their own frameworks.</li><li>Compliance is measured against the Health and Social Care Standards and the Care Inspectorate's quality framework, organised into key questions: how good is our care and support, our setting, our staffing and our leadership.</li><li>Each key question breaks into quality indicators, and services grade themselves on a six-point scale from unsatisfactory to excellent through honest, continuous self-evaluation.</li><li>Self-evaluation does not raise the grade. Acting on what it finds, through a live improvement plan, does.</li><li>Quickler runs each key question or quality indicator as a WhatsApp workflow, with one dashboard across your services. No app, no login.</li><li>Quickler captures evaluation and evidence. It is not a care record, eMAR, care management or clinical system, and holds no resident care data.</li></ul>"
